# OpenSpec Lifecycle with Engineering Governance

OpenSpec is the lifecycle owner:

```text
Explore → Propose → Apply → Verify → Sync → Archive
```

Use the native `openspec-*` Skills generated by OpenSpec. The project-local
`openspec/schemas/harness-engineering/` schema makes those workflows produce the
implementation-ready artifacts and task format required by this repository.

Each governed change lives at `openspec/changes/<change-id>/` and contains native
OpenSpec artifacts plus a Harness sidecar:

```text
.openspec.yaml
proposal.md
specs/<capability>/spec.md
design.md
tasks.md
governance.json
context-pack.md
impact-analysis.md
context-impact.json
requirement-reflection.json
approval.json
execution-evidence.json
review-evidence.json
self-refine-evidence.json
sync-evidence.json
archive-evidence.json
evidence/events.jsonl
evidence/failure-events.jsonl
evidence/lesson-preflight.json
```

After OpenSpec creates a change, run `init_governance.py` to attach
`governance.json`. Harness never creates the change directory and does not keep a
second lifecycle state. `tasks.md` is the only task definition and checkbox state;
Engineering records matching execution evidence without projecting or repairing it.

Before Apply, `approve_design.py` binds requirement/context/proposal/spec/design and
checkbox-normalized `tasks.md` digests. After Apply, `check_execution.py` verifies
that every checked OpenSpec task has a successful task run and that review file
digests match. Use `check_phase.py` for governance gates and `openspec validate
<change-id> --type change --strict --no-interactive` for OpenSpec validation.

Review must run `fitness.py --stage review --change <id> --report <path>` and bind
the report digest in `review-evidence.json`. Sync first snapshots every canonical
spec under `evidence/pre-sync/` (use an empty file when a new capability had no
canonical spec), then runs `openspec-sync-specs`, `openspec validate --specs`, and
`fitness.py --stage sync --change <id> --report <path>`. `sync-evidence.json`
binds the snapshots, delta/canonical digests, validation log, and Fitness report.
Archive is performed by `openspec-archive-change` after governance and any
production closure pass.
